Copy of cores/c128/mono/host (the host files cores/c64scpu/mono/build_mono.tcl reads), taken at commit 126c20785 (branch t182-step1, T182 step 1).
T164 3a Q1 (Alex, 2026-11-01): "Copies instead." A change in host/ does not move this core's cache key or its build; a host fix reaches
this core only by copying it in here on purpose, then update this line. The files need not equal host/ (no lint compares them).
Edits to the copies (inherited from the C128 copy, whose history this is): gideon_vhdl.tcl: the local VHDL names carry $hd/ (set by build_mono.tcl); overlay.v: the two $readmemh paths point into this folder (mem/). hdmi_enc/* and hdmi_out.v (2026-11-01, run 1134): the six forked encoder modules are renamed trx_* (hdmi -> trx_hdmi ...), because the VIC copy's vicii_kawari.v instantiates the unforked vendor hdmi and both live in one flat design.
hdmi_timing.v (2026-11-02, T164 5, first made for the C128 core): vtot_m1 is computed from the registered yact0 / vact (one clock after them) instead of the four-term sum of the row; run 1142 failed timing only there (WNS -0.095 ns, pix_mmcm, hout/mtim/row_reg[13] -> vtot_m1_reg[8]). The behaviour is the same: vtot_m1 is first read a frame line after running starts.
top.v is the base of this core's fork mono/top.v (mono/top.v.diff); the build reads mono/top.v. ultimate_sys.vhd is read with g_net = 0 (define NO_NET, T140 Q2b).
T195 (2026-11-09): ui_buttons.v added (copied from host/); top.v, ultimate_sys.vhd and pins.xdc carry the same UI_BUTTON change as host/ (Menu: left and middle, Reset: right, ITU bit 5/7 move).

